From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 109/109] PC5: small writes to a file are gathered (Wine patch 0948)

The console's kernel takes about a millisecond a write however small. Aggelos 2
saved its config 4 bytes at a time on every picture of its menus, so they drew
3 pictures a second. A synchronous write of 4 KiB or less to a regular file is
now kept and written with the ones after it at once; anything else that uses a
file writes them first.
